From 2e09ec0e5da7b3b1c692592dea8bbf165bc0fa37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukin <mylukin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 12:43:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/98] feat(cli-runner): recover from context overflow via
 /compact before minimal profile retry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When claude-cli hits a context overflow error, the new Layer 2 recovery
sequence runs before giving up:

1. Send /compact to the existing session (claude-cli only) to shrink
   conversation history. /compact supports non-interactive (-p) mode
   (supportsNonInteractive=true confirmed in claude-cli source).
2. Downgrade bootstrap profile to minimal to also shrink system prompt.
3. Retry the original prompt — using the compacted session if compact
   succeeded, or a fresh session if it failed (ensures minimal system
   prompt is injected even for systemPromptWhen:"first" backends).

Additional fixes from Codex review:
- session_expired during /compact is re-thrown immediately so the outer
  handler can clear the stale session (not silently swallowed)
- /compact is gated on isClaude: codex-cli and other backends do not
  support slash commands and must not receive "/compact" as a prompt
- isSystemCall flag on executeCliWithSession suppresses transcript writes,
  llm_output hook, and stream callbacks for the /compact invocation,
  preventing compact output from leaking to users or being recorded as
  a user turn in the session transcript

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
